{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dagger/dagger/pulls/14184","id":4554578868,"node_id":"PR_kwDODUgI1s8AAAABD3lbtA","html_url":"https://github.com/dagger/dagger/pull/14184","diff_url":"https://github.com/dagger/dagger/pull/14184.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/dagger/dagger/pull/14184.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dagger/dagger/issues/14184","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dagger/dagger/pulls/14184/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dagger/dagger/pulls/14184/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dagger/dagger/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dagger/dagger/issues/14184/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dagger/dagger/statuses/ce877b20baf492e65080805749bddff7eebd67a7","number":14184,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"fix(generate): preserve snapshots for a single generator result","user":{"login":"grouville","id":31691250,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNjkxMjUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31691250?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grouville","html_url":"https://github.com/grouville","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grouville/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grouville/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grouville/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grouville/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grouville/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grouville/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grouville/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grouville/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grouville/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"With one generator result, `dagger generate` unnecessarily merged the changeset through Git. That copied large outputs and reconstructed their snapshots, losing permission bits on exported files.\n\nUse that result's before and after snapshots directly, excluding root `.git` metadata as the merge path already does. Multiple results still use the existing conflict-checking merge. Verification of modules that could not initially load still runs before export.\n\n### Performance\n\nFresh comparison against main parent `a74ef21cb9`, using a local Dang generator that exports a **64 MiB binary file**, changes a text file, deletes a file and adds an empty directory:\n\n| Command | Main median | PR median | Faster pairs |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| `dagger generate -y` | 4.875 s | 3.033 s | 8/8 |\n\nThat is a **37.8%** wall-time reduction; median paired saving was 1.879 s. Two priming commands per engine were excluded, then eight pairs ran in alternating order, one command at a time. Each command reset the destination and changed a fixture comment. Engines used separate volumes, identical main engine binaries and runtime assets, Go 1.26.6, and a four-CPU limit. Cloud and analytics were disabled. This measures the single-result path with a large output, not a universal generation speedup.\n\nNative `wcprof` captures confirm that `Changeset.withChangesets` and `Changeset.__mergeWithChangeset` disappeared. On main their captured inclusive times were 2.19 s and 1.80 s; those times overlap and must not be added. Both captures had zero dropped events and zero open operations. Content-path computation and export remain.\n\nThe measured CLI used production commit `a4cc796f44`. Current head `533c6f5179` changes only a test assertion; production code is identical.\n\n### Correctness\n\nEvery benchmark command checked the binary's full SHA-256, changed and untouched text, deletion and preservation of `.git` metadata. The PR kept the requested `0750` binary and `0600` text permissions; main widened them to `0777` and `0666` in this local fixture. The PR also preserved the parent mode, untouched file mode and empty directory.\n\nChangeset paths retain their existing content and executable-bit semantics. A non-executable file changed only from `0644` to `0600` is not an exported path and stays `0644`. This PR preserves the snapshots of paths that are exported; it does not expand changeset path detection.\n\nThe integration regressions cover binary content, file and directory permissions, empty directories and a second no-op CLI invocation; root `.git` directory and worktree-file exclusions, including a result containing only metadata; and successful repair and verification of an initially unloadable module. The snapshot test's permission-only expectation was corrected to match the existing changeset contract.\n\nSkipping a merge when there is nothing to merge is a small change with a confirmed benefit and observable correctness improvement. No new merge implementation or cache is introduced.\n\n\nCI validation on head `533c6f5179`: all 87 Cloud checks are successful. Failed checks were retried with at most two PRs active at a time.","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-17T04:17:27Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T00:01:43Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"grouville:perf-prod-6","ref":"perf-prod-6","repo":{"id":475879762,"node_id":"R_kgDOHF1ZUg","name":"dagger","full_name":"grouville/dagger","owner":{"login":"grouville","id":31691250,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNjkxMjUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31691250?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/grouville","html_url":"https://github.com/grouville","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grouville/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grouville/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grouville/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/user